The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (!conn_info)
    return -EPROTO;
if (!ndev->target_active_prot)
    return -EINVAL;
if (test_and_set_bit(NCI_DATA_EXCHANGE, &ndev->flags))
    return -EBUSY;

Reason:
In each of these early error paths, the function nci_transceive() returns without freeing the skb that was passed by the caller, despite having taken ownership of it. This causes a memory leak, especially when these paths are hit (e.g., due to a separate bug that prevents clearing NCI_DATA_EXCHANGE).

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!conn_info) {
    kfree_skb(skb);
    return -EPROTO;
}
if (!ndev->target_active_prot) {
    kfree_skb(skb);
    return -EINVAL;
}
if (test_and_set_bit(NCI_DATA_EXCHANGE, &ndev->flags)) {
    kfree_skb(skb);
    return -EBUSY;
}

Reason:
Before each early return, the buffer is freed with kfree_skb(skb), ensuring that ownership is properly released and the memory leak is eliminated. The braces are added to group the free and return for clarity, but the essential fix is the call to kfree_skb.

